.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREDKIM-GENKEY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securedkim-genkey
.Nd generate DKIM keypair and DNS zone fragment
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar selector
.Fl d Ar domain
.Fl o Ar keyfile
.Op Fl a Ar algorithm
.Op Fl b Ar bits
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
generates a DKIM private key and writes a BIND9-compatible DNS zone fragment
beside it.
The private key is written to the file specified by
.Fl o ;
the zone fragment is written to a
.Pa .dns
file in the same directory (e.g.\&
.Pa test2026.key
produces
.Pa test2026.dns ) .
.Pp
For RSA keys the TXT record value exceeds the 255-byte character-string
limit of RFC 1035 section 3.3, so the fragment splits it into multiple
quoted strings inside parentheses.
The fragment can be
.Ic $INCLUDE Ns 'd
or pasted into a BIND9 zone for
.Ar selector Ns ._domainkey. Ns Ar domain .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s Ar selector
DKIM selector name.
Required.
This becomes part of the DNS lookup key.
.It Fl d Ar domain
Domain name the key is generated for.
Required.
.It Fl o Ar keyfile
Output path for the private key file.
Required.
The file is created with mode 0600.
.It Fl a Ar algorithm
Key algorithm:
.Dq rsa
(default) or
.Dq ed25519 .
.It Fl b Ar bits
RSA key size in bits: 2048 (default) or 4096.
Ignored for Ed25519.
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a 2048-bit RSA key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-genkey -s 2026 -d example.com -o /usr/local/etc/securedkim/example.key
.Ed
.Pp
Generate an Ed25519 key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-genkey -a ed25519 -s ed2026 -d example.com -o /usr/local/etc/securedkim/example-ed.key
.Ed
.Pp
Generate a 4096-bit RSA key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-genkey -b 4096 -s strong2026 -d example.com -o /path/to/key.pem
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT
A summary is printed to standard output naming the private key file, the
DNS record file, and the algorithm.
The DNS TXT record itself is in the
.Pa .dns
file, not on stdout.
.Pp
For RSA keys the zone fragment looks like:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
selector._domainkey.example.com. IN TXT (
    "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIIBIj..."
    "...remainder..."
    )
.Ed
.Pp
For Ed25519 keys the value fits in a single string:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
selector._domainkey.example.com. IN TXT "v=DKIM1; k=ed25519; p=..."
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-testkey 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T DomainKeys Identified Mail (DKIM) Signatures
.%R RFC 6376
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
